---
title: One support turn, text or voice - request flow
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Customer
    participant V as Voice pipeline
    participant S as SupportService
    participant G as InputGuard
    participant R as HybridRouter
    participant A as Agent
    participant T as Tools / retrieval
    participant O as OutputClaimGuard
    participant M as Session memory

    alt Voice call
        U->>V: Speaks (may interrupt the assistant)
        Note over V: WebRTC + Silero confirm speech and cancel playback, then Groq Whisper STT (one retry)
        V->>S: handle(transcript, channel="voice")
    else Text chat
        U->>S: handle(message, channel="text")
    end
    Note over S: Validate input: Unicode, size, control characters
    S->>G: check(text)
    alt Unsafe, or safety check unavailable
        G-->>S: refused
        S->>M: record refused turn (never sets verified slots)
        S-->>U: Safe refusal
    else Allowed
        G-->>S: allowed
        S->>M: snapshot (verified slots only)
        S->>R: route(text, verified hint)
        Note over R: Tier 0 rules → Tier 1 labeled examples → Tier 2 Groq LLM
        R-->>S: intent + routing source (or clarify)
        S->>A: handle(checked input)
        alt product_question
            A->>T: Hybrid retrieval (e5 + BM25, gate on best candidate)
            T-->>A: Supporting chunks
            Note over A: Groq answer with citations, or "insufficient evidence"
        else order_status
            A->>T: Groq native tool choice → read-only tool with ownership check
            T-->>A: Verified order facts
        else smalltalk, out_of_scope, unclear, escalate_to_human
            Note over A: Fixed template reply, or handoff with reference and summary
        end
        A-->>S: Reply + allowed facts
        S->>O: validate(reply, allowed facts)
        alt Unverified date, amount, order ID or promise
            O-->>S: blocked
            S-->>U: "I couldn't verify every detail in that answer"
        else Verified
            O-->>S: approved
            S->>M: record turn, update verified slots
            S-->>U: Text reply, or TTS playback on a call
        end
    end
